# 🚨 Cloud CORS & Container Memory Leak Prevention

### 1. Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) Preflight Failures

#### Problem
In deployed environments (e.g. Vercel frontend calling Render backend), browser requests fail with:
```
Access to fetch at 'https://backend.onrender.com/api/documents' from origin 'https://app.vercel.app' 
has been blocked by CORS policy: Response to preflight request doesn't pass access control check: 
No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.
```

#### Root Cause
1. In FastAPI, `CORSMiddleware` checks `allow_origins` and `allow_origin_regex`.
2. If `allow_origin_regex` only activates when `ENVIRONMENT != "production"`, or if `FRONTEND_URL` on Render is empty or missing subdomains, all OPTIONS preflights from `*.vercel.app` fail.

#### Prevention Rule
```python
# ❌ WRONG - Restricting origin regex only in development
if os.getenv("ENVIRONMENT") == "production":
    allow_origin_regex = f"^https?://{os.getenv('FRONTEND_URL')}$"

# ✅ CORRECT - Allow all Vercel preview/production domains and Render instances across all environments
allow_origin_regex = r"^https?://([a-zA-Z0-9_-]+\.)*(vercel\.app|onrender\.com|fly\.dev)(:[0-9]+)?$|^https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1)(:[0-9]+)?$"
```

